          "name": "retroarch_get_status",
          "canonical_hash": "sha256:91ba602e4084155d6b2c84e6e3b55606fff69feb0d028df163e905fcad208cf2",
          "description": "PURPOSE: Report whether RetroArch is currently playing or paused, plus the loaded system, game basename, and CRC32. USAGE: Call after retroarch_ping to learn what (if anything) is loaded; before retroarch_pause_toggle to decide whether the toggle will pause or unpause; before retroarch_frame_advance (which only steps when paused); whenever you need to confirm the previous fire-and-forget control command (pause/reset/load_state) actually took effect. For RetroArch settings (paths, flags) use retroarch_get_config instead — this tool only reports run-state and the loaded ROM identity. BEHAVIOR: No side effects — pure read of emulator status via the NCI",
          "is_mutating": false,
          "property_keys": [],
